---
import ProductLayout from "../components/ProductLayout.astro";

const faq = [
  {
    question: "When is it shipping?",
    answer:
      "In flight as of late April 2026. Email brett@alveyautomation.com to be notified the day v0.1 is published.",
  },
  {
    question: "What will it cover at v0.1?",
    answer:
      "Read-only access to the most-used QuickBooks Online endpoints: vendors, bills, customers, invoices, accounts, and the trial balance. Same shape as the SellerCloud and Walmart MCP servers, uniform JSON envelope, OAuth handled, MIT-licensed.",
  },
  {
    question: "Will it write?",
    answer:
      "No. v0.1 is read-only by design, matching the rest of the MCP server family. Write operations on accounting data have a stricter threat model and may ship as a separate package later.",
  },
  {
    question: "What auth does it use?",
    answer:
      "QuickBooks Online OAuth 2.0 (Intuit). You connect your books once, refresh tokens are stored locally and rotated automatically on near-expiry. No Alvey-hosted backend; your credentials never leave your machine.",
  },
  {
    question: "How does this differ from QBO Vendor Anomaly?",
    answer:
      "QBO Vendor Anomaly is a hosted SaaS app that runs daily and alerts you in Slack, install once, no code. The QuickBooks MCP server is a developer tool that lets Claude (or any MCP client) ask ad-hoc questions of your books in real time. Different audiences, different surfaces.",
  },
  {
    question: "Will there be a paid version?",
    answer:
      "The MCP server itself will be free / MIT, like the other MCP servers in this family. Hosted higher-level analyses (anomaly detection, cash-flow forecasting, etc.) live in their own paid marketplace apps.",
  },
];
---

<ProductLayout
  metaTitle="QuickBooks MCP: coming soon"
  metaDescription="A read-only Model Context Protocol server for QuickBooks Online. Vendors, bills, customers, invoices, accounts, trial balance. MIT-licensed, in flight."
  eyebrow="MCP Server · QuickBooks Online"
  headline="Plug Claude into your QuickBooks Online account."
  subhead="Read-only MCP server for QuickBooks Online: vendors, bills, customers, invoices, accounts, and the trial balance. Currently in flight; email below to get notified at launch."
  pricing="Free · MIT license"
  ctaLabel="Notify me at launch"
  ctaHref="mailto:brett@alveyautomation.com?subject=QuickBooks%20MCP%20availability"
  problemTitle="What you'll be able to do"
  whatYouGetTitle="Planned tool surface"
  whoForTitle="Who this is for"
  finalCtaTitle="Get notified at launch."
  finalCtaSubhead="No newsletter, no marketing list: one email when v0.1 ships."
  comingSoon={true}
  faq={faq}
>
  <Fragment slot="problem">
    <p>
      Most accounting questions are slow because the answer is buried in
      QuickBooks' UI under a report you have to remember to run. With a
      read-only MCP server wired into Claude, you'll be able to ask things
      like:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>"Show me every vendor whose bill total this month is up vs last."</li>
      <li>"Pull the open A/R aging into a markdown table."</li>
      <li>"What's the trial balance delta between the last two months?"</li>
      <li>"Find any invoices over $5,000 that have been outstanding more than 60 days."</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      No custom report. No spreadsheet export. Just a conversation.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="what-you-get">
    <p>The v0.1 surface (subject to change as it lands):</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>qbo_search_vendors</code>, by name, status, with paging</li>
      <li><code>qbo_get_vendor</code>, full vendor detail by ID</li>
      <li><code>qbo_search_bills</code>, date range, vendor, paid/unpaid filter</li>
      <li><code>qbo_get_bill</code>, full bill with line items + account splits</li>
      <li><code>qbo_search_customers</code>, by name, balance, status</li>
      <li><code>qbo_search_invoices</code>, date range, customer, paid/open</li>
      <li><code>qbo_list_accounts</code>, full chart of accounts</li>
      <li><code>qbo_get_trial_balance</code>, for any date range</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Same JSON envelope as the rest of the MCP server family. OAuth handled
      via the proven scaffold from the methodology pack, auto-refresh on
      expiry, encrypted tokens at rest, kill-switch endpoint.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="who-for">
    <p>This MCP server is for you if:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        You run QuickBooks Online and use Claude or another MCP-aware
        AI client for daily work.
      </li>
      <li>
        You'd rather ask "what's the A/R aging look like" than dig through
        Reports → Customers & Receivables → A/R Aging Detail every time.
      </li>
      <li>
        You're already a fan of the SellerCloud or Walmart MCP servers and
        want the same shape for your books.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</ProductLayout>
